# ============================================
# PUSHER CONFIGURATION (Real-time Updates)
# ============================================
# Get your credentials from: https://pusher.com/
# Create a free account and a new Channels app

# Server-side (keep secret!)
PUSHER_APP_ID=your_app_id_here
PUSHER_SECRET=your_secret_here

# Client-side (public, can be exposed)
NEXT_PUBLIC_PUSHER_KEY=your_key_here
NEXT_PUBLIC_PUSHER_CLUSTER=eu

# ============================================
# CLOUDINARY CONFIGURATION (Image Uploads)
# ============================================
# Get your credentials from: https://cloudinary.com/
# Create a free account

NEXT_PUBLIC_CLOUDINARY_CLOUD_NAME=your_cloud_name
NEXT_PUBLIC_CLOUDINARY_UPLOAD_PRESET=your_unsigned_preset

# ============================================
# SETUP INSTRUCTIONS
# ============================================

# 1. PUSHER (Real-time Inventory Updates):
#    a) Go to https://pusher.com/
#    b) Create account → Create new Channels app
#    c) Choose "EU" cluster (or your region)
#    d) Copy credentials from "App Keys" tab
#    e) Paste above
#    f) Features enabled:
#       - Real-time inventory sync across devices
#       - Multi-user collaboration
#       - Instant updates when family members add/edit items

# 2. CLOUDINARY (Product Image Uploads):
#    a) Go to https://cloudinary.com/
#    b) Create free account
#    c) Go to Settings → Upload
#    d) Create unsigned upload preset:
#       - Click "Add upload preset"
#       - Mode: "Unsigned"
#       - Preset name: e.g., "planner_inventory"
#       - Save
#    e) Copy cloud name from Dashboard
#    f) Paste above
#    g) Features enabled:
#       - Upload product photos
#       - Camera integration (mobile)
#       - CDN delivery

# 3. OPTIONAL:
#    Both features are OPTIONAL and work gracefully without configuration:
#    - Without Pusher: App works normally, no real-time sync
#    - Without Cloudinary: Can't upload images, emoji fallback works
#
#    Only add if you want these features!

# 4. RESTART:
#    After adding credentials, restart dev server:
#    npm run dev

